				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-621817#post-1979561</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-621817/da-capo-al-fine#post-1979561</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 27 Feb 2014 15:23:19 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Archereon</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1616164</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>You know, it occurs to me that &quot;Da Capo Al Fine&quot; is frequently abbreviated to D.C. Al Fine, which just so happens to be the code name of the current director of the GOC, who was hinted to be a benign &quot;type green&quot; (reality warper) in one of the GOC tales, and is &quot;known to be a European female of unknown age and nationality.&quot;</p> <p>I'm not sure what that means, but the first (somewhat ridiculous) idea that popped into my head when I made that connection was that the GOC is actually run by a alternate/parallel universe (and presumably grown up) SCP-239 who wasn't contained by the Foundation.</p> <p>My apologies for probably making a stupid wild mass guess.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
